{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.AtomWordShadow","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.AtomWordShadow","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.OrbitCount"],"declarations":23,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.orbitCount_atomShadow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.orbitCount_atomShadow","kind":"theorem","line":290,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AtomWordShadow.lean#L290-L299","doc":"**`hmerge`, PROVED from the shadow.** The atom word leaves `A + 1` orbits: the\n`A − 1` interfaces each merge exactly one pair, so `2A − (A−1) = A + 1`.\n\nThis is `ClassicalTraceFloor`'s second stated hypothesis, no longer a tabulated\ncount. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.orbitCount_freeShadow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.orbitCount_freeShadow","kind":"theorem","line":282,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AtomWordShadow.lean#L282-L288","doc":"**`hfree`, PROVED from the shadow.** The free word leaves `2A` orbits on `3A`\nstrands: `A` disjoint blocks, each costing one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.fresh_atomIdx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.fresh_atomIdx","kind":"theorem","line":250,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AtomWordShadow.lean#L250-L280","doc":"**The atom word's shadow is a fresh chain.** The right endpoints run\n`1, 3, 4, 6, 7, 9, 10, …`, strictly increasing, so each is fresh — which is exactly\nwhy every interface *merges* rather than splits. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.fresh_freeIdx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.fresh_freeIdx","kind":"theorem","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AtomWordShadow.lean#L231-L247","doc":"**The free word's shadow is a fresh chain.** Each block's right endpoint `3k+1`\nexceeds every index used by the earlier blocks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.toPairs_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.toPairs_length","kind":"theorem","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AtomWordShadow.lean#L227-L228","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.toPairs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.toPairs","kind":"def","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AtomWordShadow.lean#L223-L224","doc":"Transport an index list to transpositions of `α`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.atomIdx_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.atomIdx_lt","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AtomWordShadow.lean#L210-L219","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.freeIdx_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.freeIdx_lt","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AtomWordShadow.lean#L201-L208","doc":"Every index used by `freeIdx A` is below `3A` — the bound that makes the next\nletter's endpoint fresh. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.atomIdx_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.atomIdx_length","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AtomWordShadow.lean#L194-L199","doc":"`2A − 1` letters: `A` blocks and `A − 1` interfaces. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.freeIdx_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.freeIdx_length","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AtomWordShadow.lean#L190-L192","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.atomIdx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.atomIdx","kind":"def","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AtomWordShadow.lean#L172-L178","doc":"The atom word's shadow as index pairs, in **reverse** word order. In *word* order\nit is `swap 0 1`, then for `k = 1 … A−1` the interface `swap (3k−1) (3k)` followed by\nthe block `swap (3k) (3k+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.freeIdx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.freeIdx","kind":"def","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AtomWordShadow.lean#L163-L170","doc":"The free word's shadow as index pairs, in **reverse** word order: block `k` is\nthe transposition `(3k, 3k+1)`, and the blocks are pairwise disjoint.\n\nMeasured: each nucleon's eleven letters collapse to exactly this one transposition,\nthe same for every `k`, proton or neutron. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.orbitCount_freshProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.orbitCount_freshProd","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AtomWordShadow.lean#L141-L147","doc":"The orbit count of a fresh chain: every letter costs exactly one orbit.\n\nNo length bound is needed as a hypothesis — `orbitCount` is *defined* by this\nsubtraction, and `Fresh.length_le` shows it never truncates anyway. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Fresh.length_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Fresh.length_le","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AtomWordShadow.lean#L132-L139","doc":"A fresh chain cannot be longer than the ground set: each letter consumes a point\nthat no earlier letter touched. (Recorded rather than assumed — it is what makes the\n`ℕ` subtraction in `orbitCount_freshProd` honest, so it should be a consequence of\nfreshness, not a side hypothesis on it.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.orbitDefect_freshProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.orbitDefect_freshProd","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AtomWordShadow.lean#L113-L130","doc":"**The one lemma both counts come from.** A fresh chain of `k` transpositions has\norbit defect exactly `k`: every letter merges, none splits.\n\nEach step is `orbitDefect_swap_mul_of_not_sameCycle` (proved in `OrbitCount`), whose\n`¬ SameCycle` hypothesis is supplied by freshness via `not_sameCycle_of_apply_eq` —\nthe fresh endpoint is still a fixed point of everything applied before it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Fresh.cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Fresh.cons","kind":"ctor","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AtomWordShadow.lean#L108-L109","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Fresh.nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Fresh.nil","kind":"ctor","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AtomWordShadow.lean#L107-L107","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Fresh","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Fresh","kind":"inductive","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AtomWordShadow.lean#L103-L109","doc":"**Fresh chain.** Each pair's right endpoint is distinct from its own left endpoint\nand from every endpoint appearing later in the list — which, by the reversed reading\nof `freshProd`, means every endpoint appearing *earlier in the word*. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.freshProd_apply_eq_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.freshProd_apply_eq_self","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AtomWordShadow.lean#L93-L101","doc":"A point that is no endpoint of any pair in the list is fixed by the product. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.freshProd_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.freshProd_cons","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AtomWordShadow.lean#L90-L91","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.freshProd_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.freshProd_nil","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AtomWordShadow.lean#L88-L88","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.freshProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.freshProd","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AtomWordShadow.lean#L81-L86","doc":"The product of a list of transpositions, the head applied **last** (leftmost).\nSo the list is read in *reverse* word order, and the tail is everything that came\n*earlier* in the word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.not_sameCycle_of_apply_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.not_sameCycle_of_apply_eq","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AtomWordShadow.lean#L65-L77","doc":"A point fixed by `σ` shares no cycle with anything but itself. This is what makes\na *fresh* endpoint hand `orbitDefect_swap_mul_of_not_sameCycle` its hypothesis.\n\nStated above the `variable` line: it needs neither `Fintype` nor `DecidableEq`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}